---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="State of Stick Golf — The Tap-Connected Course" description="A tap-connected golf network bringing AI, scoring, leagues, clubhouse services, and course experiences together." eyebrow="A STATE OF STICK VERTICAL / GOLF INVESTOR BRIEF">
  <section class="pitch-hero pitch-hero-branded">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="pitch-brandbar"><div class="pitch-brand-lockup"><img src="/brand/state-of-stick-logo.svg" alt="State of Stick, Co." /><span>STATE OF STICK, CO. / GOLF VERTICAL</span></div><span class="pitch-brand-tag">BUILT TO STICK. MADE TO LAST.</span></div>
    <div class="eyebrow">THE TAP-CONNECTED COURSE</div>
    <h1>Bring intelligence<br /><em>to the fairway.</em></h1>
    <p class="page-lead">State of Stick Golf turns every course into a connected experience. A golfer taps a course marker, passport, cart, event point, or clubhouse touchpoint—and the right score, service, story, challenge, or AI guidance appears in the moment.</p>
    <div class="button-row"><a class="button" href="/round/cedar-ridge/">See the golfer experience ↗</a><a class="button secondary" href="/operator/">See the course opportunity</a></div>
      <div class="pitch-proof-row"><div class="pitch-proof-main"><img src="/brand/golf/golf-emblem.jpg" alt="State of Stick golf emblem concept" /></div><div class="pitch-proof-copy"><span class="pitch-proof-label">PHYSICAL + INTELLIGENT</span><strong>One tap connects the physical course to the digital game.</strong><small>Score the round, reach the clubhouse, join the league, ask the golf agent, and keep the memory.</small></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section shell pitch-section">
    <div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">THE SIMPLE VERSION</div><h2>One tap.<br />The whole course connected.</h2></div><p class="section-intro">The golfer gets a better round. The clubhouse gets a direct relationship. The operator gets a measurable network of places, people, play, and commerce.</p></div>
    <div class="feature-grid"><article class="feature"><span class="number">01 / PLAY</span><div><h3>Keep score and keep moving</h3><p>Record official strokes hole by hole, switch into Stableford or other formats, verify interaction at the course, and carry the round into the passport.</p></div></article><article class="feature"><span class="number">02 / CONNECT</span><div><h3>Reach the clubhouse from the course</h3><p>Tap to open course guidance, announcements, food and merchandise opportunities, event details, service requests, or the next action the golfer needs.</p></div></article><article class="feature"><span class="number">03 / COMPETE</span><div><h3>Play leagues and other golfers</h3><p>Join a season, play across participating courses, compare standings, form rivalries, and make a round count beyond the fairway where it happened.</p></div></article></div>
  </section>
  <section class="section shell connected-game-section">
    <div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">THE BIGGER IDEA</div><h2>Connect the game<br />beyond one course.</h2></div><p class="section-intro">A golfer should be able to compete with someone on another fairway, carry their history between organizations, and keep building a season after the round is over.</p></div>
    <div class="connected-game-flow"><div class="connected-node"><span>01 / PLAYER</span><h3>Own your golf record</h3><p>A passport for rounds, courses, rivalries, teams, achievements, and seasons that travels with the golfer.</p></div><div class="connected-arrow">→</div><div class="connected-node"><span>02 / ROUND</span><h3>Play anywhere</h3><p>Submit an approved round from a participating course while keeping its tees, rating, slope, rules, and evidence attached.</p></div><div class="connected-arrow">→</div><div class="connected-node"><span>03 / SEASON</span><h3>Stay in the competition</h3><p>One portable league can connect courses, workplaces, associations, charities, brands, and destinations.</p></div></div>
    <div class="connected-game-grid"><article class="feature"><span class="number">04 / SOCIAL COMPETITION</span><div><h3>Make every round count</h3><p>Follow rivals, form teams, invite friends, discover compatible leagues, and turn casual play into a reason to return.</p></div></article><article class="feature"><span class="number">05 / TRUSTED RECORDS</span><div><h3>Show how a score was established</h3><p>Self-reported, partner-attested, commissioner-approved, course-confirmed, or officially integrated—trust should be visible instead of implied.</p></div></article><article class="feature"><span class="number">06 / SHARED REWARDS</span><div><h3>Grow the game around play</h3><p>Sponsors and charities can fund transparent challenges and rewards. Regulated entry fees and payouts belong later, behind proper controls.</p></div></article></div>
    <div class="portable-season-callout"><div><div class="eyebrow">PORTABLE SEASON</div><h3>Same season. Different fairways.</h3><p>A Great Lakes league, a national ladder, or a charity challenge can expand without forcing every participant into the same club software.</p></div><a class="button" href="/league/anywhere/">See the network in motion ↗</a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="section shell ai-game-section">
    <div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">AI FOR THE CONNECTED COURSE</div><h2>Your golf agent<br />at the point of play.</h2></div><p class="section-intro">The tap is the doorway. AI is the layer that understands the golfer’s context, the course’s approved information, the league’s rules, and the clubhouse’s next action.</p></div>
    <div class="ai-game-intro"><div class="ai-orbit"><span class="ai-orbit-center">AI</span><span class="ai-orbit-node node-top">PLAYER</span><span class="ai-orbit-node node-right">COURSE</span><span class="ai-orbit-node node-bottom">SEASON</span><span class="ai-orbit-node node-left">COMMUNITY</span></div><div><div class="eyebrow">THE DIFFERENCE</div><h3>Not another chatbot.<br />A trusted golf agent.</h3><p>The agent can use State of Stick identity, physical interaction, consent, course services, events, league rules, and live conditions to coordinate a useful experience across the ecosystem.</p><p class="ai-note">Every answer should show its source, freshness, and confidence. AI can recommend and coordinate; authorized people and systems remain responsible for official scores, rules decisions, payments, safety, and prize governance.</p></div></div>
    <div class="ai-capability-grid">
      <article class="feature"><span class="number">01 / FOR THE GOLFER</span><div><h3>Your golf agent</h3><p>Find the right course, league, playing partners, event, lesson, practice plan, accessibility option, or next challenge based on the golfer’s goals and consented history.</p></div></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="number">02 / FOR THE ROUND</span><div><h3>Context at the point of play</h3><p>A tap can bring the right hole guidance, rules explanation, course announcement, clubhouse service, challenge, memory prompt, or safety notice into the moment.</p></div></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="number">03 / FOR THE SEASON</span><div><h3>Make distant competition feel present</h3><p>Explain standings, find fair matchups across courses, recommend rivalries and teams, detect incomplete records, and help commissioners run a portable season.</p></div></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="number">04 / FOR THE CLUBHOUSE</span><div><h3>Turn a tap into service</h3><p>Connect the golfer to tee-time context, event rosters, announcements, food and merchandise, service requests, and the people running the course.</p></div></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="number">05 / FOR THE GAME</span><div><h3>Open access and participation</h3><p>Use multilingual, conversational guidance to welcome beginners, families, adaptive golfers, visitors, and people who do not already know how golf works.</p></div></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="number">06 / FOR THE FUTURE</span><div><h3>Learn across the ecosystem</h3><p>With permission, aggregate patterns across courses and seasons to improve programming, sustainability, accessibility, events, and the health of the game.</p></div></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section shell pitch-proof-gallery"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">THE PRODUCT CAN BE SEEN</div><h2>From tap point<br />to golf network.</h2></div><p class="section-intro">The system is designed around real places and real moments: a golfer, a course, a league, a clubhouse, an event, a sponsor, and a physical object that makes the connection visible.</p></div><div class="pitch-gallery"><figure><img src="/brand/golf/sticklink-golf-card.jpg" alt="Connected golf emblem product card" /><figcaption>COURSE-LINKED TOUCHPOINTS</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/brand/golf/sticklink-golf-heart.jpg" alt="Heart-shaped connected golf emblem" /><figcaption>PLAYER-OWNED PASSPORT</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/brand/golf/golf-product-emblem.jpg" alt="State of Stick golf emblem product detail" /><figcaption>PHYSICAL IDENTITY FOR THE GAME</figcaption></figure></div></section>
  <section class="page shell pitch-grid">
    <div class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">BUILT NOW</div><h2>The foundation is already here.</h2><div class="record"><span class="record-dot orange"></span><div><b>Tap-connected course experience</b><small>Course and hole surfaces, physical StickLink points, tap verification, witness context, challenges, and a golfer passport are modeled and demonstrated in the pilot.</small></div></div><div class="record"><span class="record-dot green"></span><div><b>Scoring, leagues, and competition</b><small>Official strokes stay separate from Stableford, match play, skins, physical proof, and passport history. Portable seasons, standings, trust levels, and public/private league rules are defined.</small></div></div><div class="record"><span class="record-dot lime"></span><div><b>Course and network foundations</b><small>Course discovery, operator-approved map context, announcements, events, D1 persistence, API routes, and Durable Object live-state foundations connect the product surface.</small></div></div><div class="record"><span class="record-dot ink"></span><div><b>Grounded golf intelligence</b><small>A provider-neutral, provenance-aware intelligence layer can explain authorized rounds, trends, league movement, practice focus, and operator facts without inventing official results.</small></div></div></div>
    <div class="panel pitch-economics"><div class="eyebrow">NEXT BUILD</div><h2>Bring the clubhouse online.</h2><div class="economics-row"><b>AI on the course</b><span>A tap opens a grounded golf agent for hole context, rules, conditions, accessibility, pace, challenges, and the next best action.</span></div><div class="economics-row"><b>Clubhouse connectivity</b><span>Connect tee sheets, event rosters, announcements, service requests, food, merchandise, and course operations through the same physical doorway.</span></div><div class="economics-row"><b>Social play at network scale</b><span>Authenticated players, partner play, rivalries, teams, commissioner tools, cross-course leagues, and real-time standings.</span></div><div class="economics-row"><b>Partner integrations and revenue</b><span>Begin with controlled imports and webhooks, then connect tee-sheet and scoring partners while courses earn through subscriptions, events, sponsors, commerce, and physical products.</span></div><p class="pitch-note">State of Stick Golf is a network layer—not a replacement for GHIN/WHS, Golf Genius, tee-sheet software, or club-management systems. Official scores, rules, payments, safety, and prize decisions remain authoritative and human-controlled.</p></div>
    <div class="panel pitch-economics"><div class="eyebrow">HOW IT CAN MAKE MONEY</div><h2>Start useful.<br />Grow with the course.</h2><div class="economics-row"><b>Course subscriptions</b><span>Operator tools and connected touchpoints</span></div><div class="economics-row"><b>Event programs</b><span>Leagues, invitationals, challenges, and reporting</span></div><div class="economics-row"><b>Commerce revenue</b><span>Food, merchandise, offers, and sponsor attribution</span></div><div class="economics-row"><b>Physical products</b><span>Golf Passport objects, emblems, and course-linked collectibles</span></div><p class="pitch-note">The model is participation and commerce—not a betting platform. Official scores stay separate from optional formats, sponsor experiences, and passport achievements.</p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="section shell pitch-cta"><div class="eyebrow">THE ASK</div><h2>Help us put the<br />course online.</h2><p>The product foundation is built. The next step is a real pilot with golfers, a commissioner, and course operators who want one tap to connect play, the clubhouse, AI guidance, and the season around it.</p><a class="button" href="/operator/">Review the pilot surface ↗</a></section>
</Layout>
